# Binary files must never have line endings rewritten.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows treats any file it cannot prove is binary as
# text and applies LF -> CRLF on checkout. ParentVeda-Content-Brief.pdf was
# committed as "334 insertions" — Git diffed a PDF as 334 lines of text — and
# a fresh clone would have rewritten every one of those bytes, producing a file
# that no longer opens.
#
# The failure is invisible on the machine that made the commit, because its
# working copy is never touched. It only appears for the next person to clone.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.m4a   binary
*.wav   binary
*.zip   binary
*.jks   binary
*.keystore binary

# Source stays LF in the repo and is checked out however the platform wants.
*.dart  text
*.sql   text
*.md    text
*.yaml  text
*.yml   text
*.json  text

# Shell scripts and Gradle wrappers break with CRLF, whatever the platform.
*.sh          text eol=lf
gradlew       text eol=lf
